    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0731" n="617" xml:id="pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.60 f 31/21: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Einstein</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-01-12T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                                1925—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1. Your 35, September 3, 4 p.m.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d573-f1"/> Your despatch No.
                    746, December 9. Does exchange of notes of December 5 require legislative and
                    presidential approval and publication? Department wishes to publish in Treaty
                    Series as soon as all Czechoslovak formalities are completed. Your omission of
                    “indefinitely” approved.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
